        "original_id": "26ea59db-800f-5793-93d7-944af31360ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ann Wilson\n- Organizations: Hit Parader\n- Bands: Antix, Heart, Slayer, Lizzy Borden, Megadeth, Anthrax, Raven, Grim Reaper\n- Products: The Wild Bunch, Daze Gone By, Hope & Glory\n- Topics: heavy metal vocalists\n\nFacts:\n- Hit Parader was an American music magazine that operated from 1942 to 2008.\n- In 1984, Antix's song \"Daze Gone By\" appeared on Hit Parader's compilation album \"The Wild Bunch\" alongside songs by Slayer, Lizzy Borden, Megadeth, Anthrax, Raven, and Grim Reaper.\n- In 2006, Hit Parader listed Ann Wilson as one of the \"Top Heavy Metal Vocalists of All Time.\"\n- On September 11, 2007, Heart singer Ann Wilson released \"Hope & Glory,\" her first solo album.",
